  <title>Display settings</title>
  <p>
    Braille display settings control how text fits on your display and how additional
    information is marked.
  </p>
  <p>
    Contracted braille uses abbreviations for words and groups of letters, allowing more text to
    fit on the display. Orca uses liblouis translation tables to determine the symbols and
    contractions for your language.
  </p>
  <p>
    Indicator dots mark information such as links and selected text without adding words to the
    display. See "<link xref="features_text_attributes">Text attributes</link>" to choose which
    text attributes are marked.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-display-settings">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Braille</gui> category, <gui>Display Settings</gui> group.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>End of line symbol</gui>: Distinguishes the
          end of a line of text from the edge of the braille display. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Word wrap</gui>: Keeps words from being
          split across successive pans of the braille display. Default: off.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Contracted Braille</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca uses contracted braille through liblouis, a braille translation library. Default:
          off.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Expand word at cursor</gui>: Shows the word at
          the cursor in computer braille so you can inspect its individual characters while
          keeping surrounding text contracted. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Contraction Table:</gui> Selects the liblouis
          translation table Orca uses for braille symbols and contractions. Default: chosen for
          your locale.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Indicators</gui>: Controls which braille
          dots Orca uses to mark links, selections, and text attributes. These indicators are
          shown like underlining on the braille display.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Hyperlink:</gui> Selects the dot or
              dots Orca uses to mark text that is part of a link. Choices: None, Dot 7, Dot 8,
              Dots 7 and 8 (default).
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Selection:</gui> Selects the dot or
              dots Orca uses to mark selected text. Choices: None, Dot 7, Dot 8, Dots 7 and 8
              (default).
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Text Attributes:</gui> Selects the dots
              used to mark text attributes in braille, like underlining. The same indicator is
              used for all attributes enabled for braille; it shows where an attribute is
              present, rather than which attribute it is. Choosing no indicator hides the
              markers. Choices: None (default), Dot 7, Dot 8, Dots 7 and 8.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
